{
  "$comment": [
    "INDOX's DISPLAY CATALOG — the one place a human writes how this app's data reads.",
    "",
    "WHAT THIS IS. Every Hebrew word the UI puts on a column header, a status pill, a type bar or",
    "a filter option comes from here. It is merged into the repo schema by",
    "scripts/ops/gen-indox-schema.py, so `GET /repos/<r>` serves structure AND presentation",
    "together and no screen keeps a private label map. Add a label here and it is live on the next",
    "page load, with no frontend change.",
    "",
    "WHY IT EXISTS. Four screens each spelled these enums differently and the grid rendered raw SQL",
    "identifiers as headers, so a column added to the pipeline reached the operator as an English",
    "shout (IRRELEVANT, API_TOOLS_FAILED, SOURCE_TYPE) and fixing it meant editing every screen.",
    "",
    "RULES.",
    "  * Labels are DISPLAY ONLY. The raw enum is what is filtered, written and stored.",
    "  * An unlabelled column still renders — as its raw name. A new column must be visible and",
    "    usable the day it appears, never blank.",
    "  * `deprecated: true` hides a column from the default view but KEEPS it declared. A column",
    "    that exists and is undeclared is the failure this file ends; hiding by omission recreates it.",
    "  * The COLUMN LIST is generated from the live table, not hand-maintained here. This file only",
    "    says how the columns that exist should read.",
    "",
    "Run `python3 scripts/ops/gen-indox-schema.py --check` to fail when the table has a column the",
    "schema does not declare."
  ],
